## Code rules

- 2-space indent
- Explicit access control (`public`, `internal`, `private`)
- `@Observable @MainActor` for ViewModels — no `ObservableObject`
- `async/await` only — no `DispatchQueue`
- Sorted imports
- No `print` / `fatalError` / force-unwrap
- Never add `// swiftlint:disable` — fix the root cause

## Architecture

This project uses **__ARCHITECTURE_NAME__**. The module dependency direction is `Features → Core → External`. Never invert.

See `README.md` for module map.

## Don't

- Don't edit `*.xcodeproj` / `*.xcworkspace` directly — they're generated from `__CONFIG_FILE__`
- Don't introduce UIKit, Storyboards, or XIBs — SwiftUI only
- Don't introduce a new external dependency without checking if Foundation / Swift stdlib covers it
- Don't widen access control just to make tests pass — use `@testable import`
